WEBVTT

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:16.110
<i>Adam Ward, CEO of SETTEN, the world's 
largest internet service company,</i>

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:19.620
<i>came to Japan to gain information 
on the anisotropic being.</i>

00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:26.080
<i>Adam hired Gonno Takumi of NNK 
to interview Yaha-kui zaShunina.</i>

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:30.710
<i>Gonno and his crew were invited inside Kado,</i>

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:35.840
<i>where they saw the Sansa, a device that 
gives humanity a sense of the anisotropic</i>

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:37.270
<i>and makes sleep unnecessary.</i>

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:45.740
<i>Meanwhile, negotiator Tsukai Saraka 
told Shindo Kojiro what she wanted.</i>

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:49.350
I want to send Yaha-kui zaShunina 
back to the anisotropic.

00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:25.160
Talnel

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:29.840
They're going to broadcast 
the footage of the Sansa?

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:32.670
That footage affects the human brain.

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:36.240
What's going to happen 
if they broadcast that?

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:38.220
Some people could get sick!

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:41.680
We were fine, though.

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:44.760
There were only three of us!
That doesn't guarantee anything!

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:46.350
I think it'll be fine.

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:48.950
Gonno-san, you can tell 
by the feel of it, right?

00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:51.850
All it means is that 
you're able to not sleep.

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:53.250
What if...

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:55.960
What if it's not just that?

00:02:55.960 --> 00:02:57.570
How do we take responsibility?

00:02:57.570 --> 00:03:01.090
Then why did we come here?

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:03.190
Well...

00:03:03.190 --> 00:03:05.870
You always worry too much, boss.

00:03:11.070 --> 00:03:12.540
Yaha-kui zaShunina!

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:16.840
Can we contact the outside from here?

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:23.220
<b>Hail to Humanity 

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:26.260
<i>The Sansa?</i>

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:32.690
Yaha-kui zaShunina wants us to use our 
fullest power to share it with humanity.

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:36.280
It's too dangerous.

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:37.530
Bishop...

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:40.140
With the Wam, it was just the creation method.

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:42.830
But this time, you change 
the instant you see it.

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:46.070
This is video terrorism.

00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:49.540
Gonno, your thoughts?

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:50.990
We should broadcast it.

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:52.620
Insanity!

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:55.460
Of course, we'll warn people first.

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:58.370
We'll declare what it is and have 
them confirm they want to watch.

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:01.630
But the final decision rests 
with the individual.

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:04.260
I want to leave it up to the will of humanity.

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:05.800
Why do you feel that way?

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:09.870
Both TV and the internet are just 
methods to share information.

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:12.670
A true information network
can only be created if

00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:15.100
there's someone to share it 
and someone to receive it.

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:18.680
<i>We are the ones who have 
chosen to share information,</i>

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:21.530
<i>so we mustn't run from that.</i>

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:25.780
So, get this, Gonno.

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:30.040
The whole company told me 
it was a waste of money,

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:34.330
but last year, we at SETTEN 
got ourselves a satellite.

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:35.970
A satellite?

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:39.340
Which means...

00:04:41.390 --> 00:04:43.710
Simultaneous worldwide broadcast.

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:48.020
Yes, I'll call back as soon 
as I have confirmation.

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:49.270
Yes, yes!

00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:50.680
Yes. Yes.

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:52.510
Goodbye.

00:04:56.620 --> 00:04:57.600
Please.

00:04:58.810 --> 00:05:02.530
Let me have Shindo-san for one day.

00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:06.090
What does that mean?

00:05:06.090 --> 00:05:10.040
I want to negotiate with 
him, as an individual.

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:15.290
I'm aware that this is the most critical 
moment of this whole endeavor.

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:18.110
But please, just one day...

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:19.570
Sure.

00:05:20.450 --> 00:05:22.340
I'll handle things here.

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:27.790
We can handle things for a day 
while you two aren't here.

00:05:27.790 --> 00:05:29.330
Right, Natsume-san?

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:31.310
I'm heading back, actually.

00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:34.150
Bu— Wait!

00:05:34.150 --> 00:05:35.340
I can't do this myself!

00:05:35.340 --> 00:05:36.760
No way!

00:05:36.760 --> 00:05:37.880
Hanamori-san.

00:05:37.880 --> 00:05:39.370
Thank you.

00:05:41.210 --> 00:05:43.710
I can't do this without you, Natsume-san!

00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:43.710
Tsukai-san.

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:44.740
Come on, Natsume-san!

00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:47.170
I'll treat you to some sake!

00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:48.740
Shindo-kun is an unparalleled negotiator.

00:05:47.170 --> 00:05:48.740
Come on, please!

00:05:49.060 --> 00:05:52.920
But you're the Ministry of
Foreign Affairs' ace, as well.

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:50.650
No.

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:52.450
Take responsibility and do your best.

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:55.060
Oh, come on, I'm begging you!

00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:55.750
Have a good negotiation.

00:05:55.060 --> 00:05:56.930
Not happening.

00:05:56.930 --> 00:05:59.040
Natsume-san!

00:06:01.490 --> 00:06:04.790
Okay, gotta hang in there just a little longer.

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:16.730
Good morning.

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:17.950
Morning.

00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:20.820
Sorry to have you come all the way here.

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:26.570
Chestnut

00:06:25.470 --> 00:06:26.570
Is something wrong?

00:06:28.890 --> 00:06:29.620
No.

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:31.870
Let's go, then. This way.

00:06:36.190 --> 00:06:39.000
I'm not actually sure what 
I'm doing here today...

00:06:40.510 --> 00:06:41.980
Where are we going?

00:06:41.980 --> 00:06:43.890
My parents' house, first.

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:46.990
Your parents'?

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:51.090
<b>Kazari</b>

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:51.090
I'm back!

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:53.000
Are you guys home?

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:56.600
Is that you, Saraka?

00:06:56.600 --> 00:06:58.420
What's all this about?

00:07:01.060 --> 00:07:02.920
Dad! Dad!

00:07:05.560 --> 00:07:10.310
Our mother is away, 
so we can't offer you much.

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:13.660
This senbei is good.

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:15.270
Shindo-san, you have some, too.

00:07:16.010 --> 00:07:17.200
Thanks.

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:20.750
I can't believe it's the famous 
Shindo Kojiro-san, though.

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:22.760
Why is that so hard to believe?

00:07:22.760 --> 00:07:24.810
Well, he's famous!

00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:26.450
I've seen him a ton of times on TV!

00:07:26.450 --> 00:07:28.210
I was on TV, too!

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:30.440
Only at the very beginning.

00:07:30.440 --> 00:07:32.100
I only saw you at the airport.

00:07:32.100 --> 00:07:34.030
Yeah, but...

00:07:34.030 --> 00:07:37.760
I'm still amazed you managed 
to pull it off, though.

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:40.050
To be honest, I underestimated you.

00:07:40.050 --> 00:07:41.250
What do you mean?

00:07:43.740 --> 00:07:47.020
But it kind of makes me tear up, you know?

00:07:49.060 --> 00:07:50.990
Why...

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:50.990
Shindo-san.

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:52.030
Yes?

00:07:53.100 --> 00:07:58.430
She's never been able to cook or clean at all,

00:07:59.490 --> 00:08:02.850
but she doesn't really like to 
dress up and look nice, either.

00:08:04.450 --> 00:08:06.570
I gave up and left her to her own devices,

00:08:06.570 --> 00:08:10.130
and she ran off overseas on her own.

00:08:11.230 --> 00:08:15.980
She's a tomboy, and the most 
stubborn girl I've ever known,

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:19.900
but she's still my precious daughter.

00:08:22.110 --> 00:08:28.090
Shindo-san... please take 
care of my daughter.

00:08:28.550 --> 00:08:30.770
I'm so happy for you, Saraka...

00:08:30.770 --> 00:08:32.100
Dad, no!

00:08:32.100 --> 00:08:33.570
It's not like that!

00:08:33.570 --> 00:08:36.210
Hey, Shindo-san, you say something, too!

00:08:33.570 --> 00:08:36.700
Come home to visit us sometimes, you hear?

00:08:36.210 --> 00:08:39.420
As your dad says, we're working 
together on the anisotropic problem—

00:08:39.420 --> 00:08:44.520
No! I'm telling you, this 
isn't what you think it is!

00:08:40.050 --> 00:08:43.460
Your happiness is our happiness, Saraka...

00:08:48.180 --> 00:08:49.260
Sheesh.

00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:52.630
You can be so thoughtless.

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:56.010
If he's just a coworker, 
why didn't you say so?

00:08:56.010 --> 00:08:59.100
You're the one who got the wrong idea!

00:09:00.170 --> 00:09:02.900
And then you want to see 
me doing my engraving?

00:09:02.900 --> 00:09:07.710
Everything you do just 
comes out of the blue.

00:09:08.850 --> 00:09:14.130
Shindo-san, she's causing you 
a lot of trouble, isn't she?

00:09:15.090 --> 00:09:18.490
If it weren't for Saraka-san, Japan 
wouldn't be functioning right now.

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:19.930
Her?

00:09:19.930 --> 00:09:21.470
What?

00:09:38.050 --> 00:09:40.370
It's called "kazari kanagu," 
metal fixture decorations.

00:09:40.370 --> 00:09:43.350
Our family's been doing this for generations.

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:44.790
"Kazari kanagu"?

00:09:46.410 --> 00:09:51.150
The metal decorations that you see 
at shrines, or religious artifacts.

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:52.790
I see.

00:09:53.220 --> 00:09:56.650
I didn't realize that they 
were all handmade, though.

00:09:56.650 --> 00:09:59.890
There aren't many left who can make them...

00:10:01.230 --> 00:10:03.160
Did something bad happen?

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:09.030
The only times you come to my workshop are 
usually when something's got you down.

00:10:10.450 --> 00:10:11.350
Nope.

00:10:13.030 --> 00:10:14.190
I see.

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:27.230
Looks like they're starting something big.

00:10:28.270 --> 00:10:29.970
Is this gonna be okay?

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:36.020
Even if it's not, we can't stop it.

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:41.230
On the other side of the line
is anisotropic jurisdiction.

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:46.290
It's almost like it's alive...

00:10:46.770 --> 00:10:50.480
Shindo-san, have you ever seen a dragon?

00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:51.470
A real one?

00:10:51.470 --> 00:10:52.230
Yes.

00:10:52.230 --> 00:10:52.950
No.

00:10:54.550 --> 00:10:56.320
Me, neither.

00:10:56.320 --> 00:10:58.580
They're imaginary, anyway.

00:11:00.830 --> 00:11:04.850
Humans imagine dragons,
engrave them into metal,

00:11:06.590 --> 00:11:09.390
and we feel as if that mere metal is alive.

00:11:10.360 --> 00:11:12.920
That's part of what makes us human.

00:11:14.090 --> 00:11:16.780
All of that is what humans do.

00:11:21.550 --> 00:11:25.570
I've loved aquariums and 
zoos since I was little.

00:11:25.570 --> 00:11:29.510
I begged my parents into taking 
me to them dozens of times.

00:11:31.670 --> 00:11:33.540
I like animals, too.

00:11:34.730 --> 00:11:39.660
On the evolutionary tree, jellyfish 
were one of the earliest branches.

00:11:39.660 --> 00:11:43.680
They're said to be similar in 
appearance to the first animals.

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:45.870
The first animals?

00:11:45.870 --> 00:11:48.020
If you follow human 
evolution back a long way,

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:50.310
we once looked like this.

00:11:50.760 --> 00:11:53.060
I can't imagine it at all.

00:11:53.720 --> 00:12:00.320
Life has been splitting off, evolving, 
and spreading since the distant past.

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:02.140
And it was natural.

00:12:02.140 --> 00:12:04.910
Everything happened naturally.

00:12:05.940 --> 00:12:08.010
Nobody made it.

00:12:08.630 --> 00:12:10.460
Nobody's will was involved.

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:14.920
Nature was born naturally,

00:12:17.100 --> 00:12:20.460
and that's a miracle.

00:12:25.400 --> 00:12:30.210
I rode the water bus many times 
with my friends in high school.

00:12:31.220 --> 00:12:34.390
I loved the way Tokyo looked from here.

00:12:35.370 --> 00:12:37.230
It was so crowded and messy,

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:40.390
with all the good things and 
bad things crammed together.

00:12:40.390 --> 00:12:43.620
I loved how it looked like a toy box.

00:12:46.370 --> 00:12:52.200
I think negotiation is about understanding 
someone, and having them understand you.

00:12:52.570 --> 00:12:54.170
Mutual understanding.

00:12:54.170 --> 00:12:56.960
It's an absolute necessity for negotiation.

00:12:58.810 --> 00:13:00.730
What I showed you today

00:13:00.730 --> 00:13:02.760
is the path of my life.

00:13:03.510 --> 00:13:09.650
I wanted you to know me, so that 
you can understand how I think.

00:13:11.880 --> 00:13:14.730
Is this about you wanting to send 
zaShunina back to the anisotropic?

00:13:15.930 --> 00:13:18.730
It's not that I dislike the anisotropic being.

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:22.470
The technology itself of 
the Wam and the Sansa

00:13:22.470 --> 00:13:25.490
is doubtlessly a benefit 
for humanity. I realize that.

00:13:26.550 --> 00:13:28.330
Why, then?

00:13:28.330 --> 00:13:31.490
Because there's something more 
important than the benefits.

00:13:32.690 --> 00:13:34.990
And it's this place.

00:13:37.690 --> 00:13:38.750
This place?

00:13:42.490 --> 00:13:43.320
The universe.

00:13:44.860 --> 00:13:48.050
Where dust gathered and galaxies were born,

00:13:48.050 --> 00:13:51.380
where stars were born, 
and where Earth was born.

00:13:52.680 --> 00:13:55.720
On that Earth, tiny lives were born,

00:13:55.720 --> 00:13:59.940
and they flourished, and were 
destroyed, and survived,

00:13:59.940 --> 00:14:02.210
until at last, humanity was born.

00:14:03.460 --> 00:14:05.410
Humanity created civilization,

00:14:05.410 --> 00:14:09.130
built cities, and developed culture,

00:14:09.130 --> 00:14:11.030
and we remain alive to this day.

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:14.880
All of that happened here in this universe.

00:14:14.880 --> 00:14:16.550
Not in the anisotropic.

00:14:17.910 --> 00:14:19.700
It doesn't belong to the anisotropic.

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:23.740
This place belongs to us.

00:14:24.810 --> 00:14:28.130
It's not something that Yaha-kui 
zaShunina can be allowed to destroy.

00:14:28.900 --> 00:14:31.470
It belongs to us?

00:14:32.820 --> 00:14:35.630
I want to protect the dignity of humanity,

00:14:35.630 --> 00:14:37.730
and of the world.

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:39.550
What I...

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:44.330
What we treasure.

00:14:51.160 --> 00:14:54.450
I don't know how they built 
something like this so fast.

00:14:54.450 --> 00:14:58.850
It's a next-generation construction 
method that we used to make SETTEN's HQ.

00:14:58.850 --> 00:15:01.790
It's flexible enough that it can be 
quickly dismantled and moved.

00:15:02.160 --> 00:15:06.170
Gonno, today's broadcast will be 
done online and via satellite.

00:15:06.170 --> 00:15:08.420
It'll be the largest in the world.

00:15:08.890 --> 00:15:10.740
Estimated views are at...

00:15:11.880 --> 00:15:14.020
2.5 billion.

00:15:15.190 --> 00:15:18.200
Are we moving too fast?

00:15:18.200 --> 00:15:22.850
I don't know the speed at which
humanity should advance.

00:15:23.370 --> 00:15:26.200
Maybe we should go slower.

00:15:26.740 --> 00:15:29.650
Maybe we should go a hundred times faster.

00:15:30.220 --> 00:15:32.040
So I want to try both.

00:15:33.310 --> 00:15:35.830
Humanity can slow down on its own,

00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:39.580
but if we want to go faster, 
we need the anisotropic's power.

00:15:40.740 --> 00:15:42.750
Now's the time to put the pedal to the metal.

00:15:44.790 --> 00:15:47.340
I've no intention of stopping 
the Sansa broadcast.

00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:54.070
<i>I've told the police and ambulances to 
be on standby when the broadcast occurs.</i>

00:15:54.950 --> 00:15:57.980
<i>This is a worldwide broadcast 
via the internet and satellite.</i>

00:15:58.510 --> 00:16:01.060
<i>Nobody can stop it.</i>

00:16:02.120 --> 00:16:03.270
Shindo, listen to me.

00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:04.310
Yes, sir.

00:16:05.050 --> 00:16:07.240
<i>I am the prime minister of Japan.</i>

00:16:07.890 --> 00:16:12.530
<i>I'll do everything I can to protect 
Japan, and the people here.</i>

00:16:13.370 --> 00:16:17.180
SETTEN is acting in accordance 
with its own philosophy, too.

00:16:17.990 --> 00:16:22.200
Right now, everyone in the world 
is fighting in their own way,

00:16:22.200 --> 00:16:24.250
amidst the chaos of the anisotropic.

00:16:25.480 --> 00:16:28.470
<i>But Shindo, you are free.</i>

00:16:29.380 --> 00:16:33.890
<i>You told us that the position the government 
offered you would just bind you.</i>

00:16:35.290 --> 00:16:37.890
That's what impresses me about you.

00:16:39.010 --> 00:16:41.150
<i>We need the way you can maintain</i>

00:16:41.150 --> 00:16:45.270
<i>your individuality, without 
being influenced by anyone.</i>

00:16:45.900 --> 00:16:49.150
<i>Do as you see fit, Shindo.</i>

00:16:53.850 --> 00:16:59.130
<i>The special program by networking company 
SETTEN will start after this, at 8:00 PM,</i>

00:16:59.130 --> 00:17:02.080
<i>as a live broadcast by NNK.</i>

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:04.980
<i>This broadcast is planned 
to contain an appearance</i>

00:17:04.980 --> 00:17:08.370
<i>by Yaha-kui zaShunina, the anisotropic being.</i>

00:17:08.370 --> 00:17:09.590
<i>I repeat:</i>

00:17:09.590 --> 00:17:13.590
<i>The special program by networking company 
SETTEN will start after this, at 8:00 PM,</i>

00:17:13.590 --> 00:17:16.140
<i>as a live broadcast by NNK.</i>

00:17:19.950 --> 00:17:27.960
This broadcast will contain footage of
a special device given to us by the anisotropic. 

00:17:29.450 --> 00:17:32.740
It is now 8:00 PM, Japan time.

00:17:30.330 --> 00:17:48.480
This broadcast will contain footage of a special device given to us by the anisotropic. 
<b>Viewing this device may have unexpected effects on the human body.</b>
Please keep this in mind if you wish to continue viewing.

00:17:32.740 --> 00:17:35.340
I am Gonno Takumi, with SETTEN.

00:17:36.150 --> 00:17:41.950
We will now share a message from the 
anisotropic being to everyone in the world.

00:17:48.480 --> 00:19:53.310
<b>Emergency Press Conference by Yaha-kui zaShunina, the anisotropic being 
After this, a new device separate from the Wam will be revealed</b>

00:17:53.270 --> 00:17:56.380
Yaha-kui zaShunina, the anisotropic being.

00:17:56.380 --> 00:18:00.870
What is it you wish to 
share with humanity today?

00:18:03.260 --> 00:18:07.500
I have brought another device, 
separate from the Wam,

00:18:07.500 --> 00:18:09.470
into this universe.

00:18:10.270 --> 00:18:14.890
It affects the human consciousness and senses.

00:18:14.890 --> 00:18:17.790
I call it the Sansa.

00:18:18.790 --> 00:18:24.630
What exactly do you mean when you say 
it affects consciousness and senses?

00:18:25.530 --> 00:18:27.050
By seeing the Sansa,

00:18:27.050 --> 00:18:32.420
humanity can gain a sense of the anisotropic.

00:18:30.350 --> 00:19:53.310
A Message from the Anisotropic to Humanity
<b>The new device's name is "Sansa"</b>

00:18:33.430 --> 00:18:36.660
This causes several changes,

00:18:36.660 --> 00:18:38.510
one of which is that

00:18:38.510 --> 00:18:41.650
you will no longer need to sleep.

00:18:42.490 --> 00:18:47.780
You mean we won't have to sleep to survive?

00:18:49.380 --> 00:18:51.880
Here in the universe, humans are

00:18:51.880 --> 00:18:55.380
only aware of a portion of what they truly are.

00:18:56.420 --> 00:18:58.820
Gaining a sense of the anisotropic

00:18:58.820 --> 00:19:01.200
will expand humanity.

00:19:01.740 --> 00:19:03.530
It is possible to allow

00:19:03.530 --> 00:19:06.620
that expanded region to sleep for you.

00:19:07.340 --> 00:19:09.000
Humans spend an average

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:11.210
of eight hours a day asleep,

00:19:11.800 --> 00:19:15.540
and during that time, human activity ceases.

00:19:16.430 --> 00:19:20.110
Avoiding this will bring humanity

00:19:20.110 --> 00:19:22.340
closer to the right answer.

00:19:22.340 --> 00:19:25.010
I want to ask you, Anisotropic Being.

00:19:25.010 --> 00:19:27.060
What is "the right answer"?

00:19:29.650 --> 00:19:32.150
There are problems in the world.

00:19:32.150 --> 00:19:33.550
Solving those problems

00:19:33.550 --> 00:19:35.310
is the meaning of the world.

00:19:36.430 --> 00:19:39.490
Humanity must solve these problems.

00:19:40.050 --> 00:19:42.370
It must get close to the right answer.

00:19:43.390 --> 00:19:46.370
The Sansa exists for that purpose.

00:19:46.830 --> 00:19:49.880
The Sansa will now be shown.

00:19:50.410 --> 00:19:51.950
It's expected to have various

00:19:51.950 --> 00:19:53.650
effects on the human body.

00:19:53.310 --> 00:20:01.030
This broadcast will contain footage of a special device given to us by the anisotropic. 
<b>Viewing this device may have unexpected effects on the human body.</b>
Please keep this in mind if you wish to continue viewing.

00:19:53.650 --> 00:19:58.460
I repeat: if you are concerned, 
please do not watch.

00:19:59.430 --> 00:20:00.470
Kado.

00:20:14.820 --> 00:20:19.190
<i>The Sansa will open new 
possibilities for humanity.</i>

00:20:20.450 --> 00:20:26.950
I hope that what waits beyond them 
will bring happiness to the anisotropic,

00:20:26.950 --> 00:20:28.780
<i>and to humanity.</i>

00:20:36.110 --> 00:20:40.550
The anisotropic being has 
gained the power of the media.

00:20:41.130 --> 00:20:42.960
The changes will spread faster,

00:20:42.960 --> 00:20:45.970
like a burning wildfire.

00:20:48.390 --> 00:20:51.430
Can we endure this?

00:21:04.250 --> 00:21:09.610
A more wonderful world than we have 
now waits beyond this revolution.

00:21:09.610 --> 00:21:11.700
That's what I believed, but...

00:21:12.600 --> 00:21:14.430
Now, I'm a little uncertain.

00:21:15.780 --> 00:21:19.910
That's why I'm going to talk to zaShunina.

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:21.920
Shindo-san...

00:21:28.980 --> 00:21:29.720
zaShunina!

00:21:43.140 --> 00:21:46.650
Isn't there some other way to do that?

00:21:48.570 --> 00:21:49.160
What's that?

00:21:50.910 --> 00:21:53.580
Can we talk for a bit, zaShunina?

00:21:54.930 --> 00:21:57.820
I wanted to speak to you, as well,

00:22:01.910 --> 00:22:03.000
Shindo.

00:23:36.510 --> 00:23:38.640
I have a bad feeling, somehow.

00:23:38.640 --> 00:23:41.890
But some people view this 
change as destruction.

00:23:41.890 --> 00:23:42.560
Kado.

00:23:42.920 --> 00:23:43.780
The Wam.

00:23:43.780 --> 00:23:44.830
The Sansa.

00:23:44.830 --> 00:23:46.540
And the fourth device...

00:23:46.540 --> 00:23:49.530
Are you... God?

00:23:48.550 --> 00:23:52.000
Nanomis-hein
